.TH PEIOS-INSTALL 1 "September 2026" "Peios" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
peios-install \- install the running Peios system onto a disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peios-install --yes
.I ESP_PARTITION ROOT_PARTITION
.br
.B peios-install --yes --whole-disk
.RB [ --force ]
.I DISK
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peios-install
formats the selected EFI system partition as FAT32 and the root partition as
ext4, copies the running system, and replaces the target's live-boot packages
with disk-boot packages from the installation medium.
It rebuilds the target initramfs and writes a unified kernel image to
.B EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
on the EFI system partition. No firmware boot entry is created.
.PP
With
.BR --whole-disk ,
it first creates a partition table, a 512 MiB EFI system partition, and a
root partition occupying the remaining space.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --yes
Confirm destructive installation. This option is required; there is no
interactive confirmation. Existing contents of both target partitions are lost.
.TP
.B --whole-disk
Partition the named disk before installation. Existing disk contents are lost.
.TP
.B --force
Allow replacement of a partition table that the partitioning tool would
otherwise refuse to replace. Valid only with
.BR --whole-disk .
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage and exit with status 2.
.PP
Place options before device operands. Devices must be direct names under
.BR /dev ,
not paths through
.BR /dev/disk/by-id .
The EFI system and root partitions must differ and must not be mounted.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Run from a Peios system with the permissions required to partition, format,
mount, copy protected files, and update the registry. The installer does not
perform a Unix user-ID check.
The installation medium must configure the
.B peios-medium
package repository and supply the disk-boot packages.
The source system must have exactly one kernel under
.B /usr/lib/modules/*/vmlinuz-*
and a readable
.BR /system/boot/initramfs.cpio.zst .
.SH WARNINGS
This command destroys data. Check all device names and keep backups before
using it. It is not a dry-run tool and does not roll back a failed installation.
.PP
The running system's data, accounts, and credentials are copied. The installer
retires the live first-account provisioning service in the running registry,
but does not change an existing development account's known password.
Change inherited credentials before treating the installed system as secure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /run/peios-install
Working directory containing the target root and EFI partition mountpoints.
.TP
.B /lcl/etc/boot/cmdline
Kernel command line generated in the target from its disk-boot template and
root filesystem UUID.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates completion. Invalid invocation prints usage with status 2.
Other failures return a nonzero status; inspect the diagnostic before retrying.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peipkg (1),
.BR mkfs.vfat (8),
.BR mke2fs (8)
